{"nodes": [{"id": "aigen_backend_docs_bug_analysis_issue_99_vd_expiry_s3_dic_issue_99", "label": "Issue 99 VD Expiry S3 PoV DIC", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bug-analysis-issue-99-vd-expiry-s3-dic.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_bug_analysis_issue_99_vd_expiry_s3_dic_bug_1_dic_detail_sequence_mixing", "label": "Bug 1 DIC Detail Sequence Mixing", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "listItemRFQDIC filters on rfq_number, vendor_batch and statuses but never on vendor_sequence, so an S3 item grouped by item_code surfaces inside an S2 detail view; the dashboard query already had the exclusion logic the detail query lacked.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bug-analysis-issue-99-vd-expiry-s3-dic.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_bug_analysis_issue_99_vd_expiry_s3_dic_bug_2_premature_dic_email", "label": "Bug 2 Premature DIC Email", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "In parallel mode the two vendors sit in different vendor_batch values after a DIC revise cycle, so a check scoped to the submitting vendor batch finds zero pending vendors and sends the DIC email while the sibling has not answered.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bug-analysis-issue-99-vd-expiry-s3-dic.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_bug_analysis_issue_99_vd_expiry_s3_dic_bug_3_need_action_vs_waiting_vendor", "label": "Bug 3 Need Action vs Waiting Vendor", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The S3 branch of toUserFlatRow followed milestone_id alone while the S1 and S2 branches already consulted sv_group, so a partially submitted parallel card claimed Need Action; the fix reuses data the query already returns instead of adding a subquery.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bug-analysis-issue-99-vd-expiry-s3-dic.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_bug_analysis_issue_99_vd_expiry_s3_dic_bug_4_card_grouping", "label": "Bug 4 Separate S3 Cards Without Context", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The dashboard GROUP BY emits one card per vendor state, so the same item code in the same sequence renders as two disconnected cards with no cross-vendor context.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bug-analysis-issue-99-vd-expiry-s3-dic.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_bug_analysis_issue_99_vd_expiry_s3_dic_check_pending_rfq_with_multiple_vendors", "label": "checkPendingRfqWithMultipleVendors", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Asks whether two or more vendors are pending in one batch; both the batch scope and the threshold of two are wrong for parallel mode, where the real question is whether any sibling of the same item_code in the same sequence is still pending.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bug-analysis-issue-99-vd-expiry-s3-dic.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_bug_analysis_issue_99_vd_expiry_s3_dic_should_send_to_dic", "label": "shouldSendToDic Decision", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "A single boolean for the whole submission, so one waiting S3 item would otherwise also hold back the S2 items submitted alongside it.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bug-analysis-issue-99-vd-expiry-s3-dic.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_bug_analysis_issue_99_vd_expiry_s3_dic_sv_group", "label": "sv_group Aggregate", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "MIN over status_vendor with ACCEPTED and NEED_CONFIRMATION folded to 1 yields PENDING whenever any grouped vendor has not submitted, which is exactly the sibling signal the dashboard needs.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bug-analysis-issue-99-vd-expiry-s3-dic.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_bug_analysis_issue_99_vd_expiry_s3_dic_list_item_rfq_dic", "label": "listItemRFQDIC Query", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bug-analysis-issue-99-vd-expiry-s3-dic.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_bug_analysis_issue_99_vd_expiry_s3_dic_to_user_flat_row", "label": "toUserFlatRow Status Mapper", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bug-analysis-issue-99-vd-expiry-s3-dic.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_bug_analysis_issue_99_vd_expiry_s3_dic_vendor_batch_divergence", "label": "Vendor Batch Divergence After DIC Revise", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "vendor_batch increments before an item is re-sent, so repeated revise cycles leave the two parallel vendors in different batches; measured at 83 percent of S3 rows still matching, which is why the bug looked intermittent.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bug-analysis-issue-99-vd-expiry-s3-dic.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_bug_analysis_issue_99_vd_expiry_s3_dic_expired_vendor_cron_mitigation", "label": "handleExpiredVendor Delay Mitigation", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Holding an item back while a sibling is pending risks it never being sent; the expiry cron converts a silent vendor to RFQ_NOT_SUBMITTED, which removes the pending sibling and releases the DIC email.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bug-analysis-issue-99-vd-expiry-s3-dic.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "aigen_backend_docs_bug_analysis_issue_99_vd_expiry_s3_dic_issue_99", "target": "aigen_backend_docs_bug_analysis_issue_99_vd_expiry_s3_dic_bug_1_dic_detail_sequence_mixing", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bug-analysis-issue-99-vd-expiry-s3-dic.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "aigen_backend_docs_bug_analysis_issue_99_vd_expiry_s3_dic_issue_99", "target": "aigen_backend_docs_bug_analysis_issue_99_vd_expiry_s3_dic_bug_2_premature_dic_email", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bug-analysis-issue-99-vd-expiry-s3-dic.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "aigen_backend_docs_bug_analysis_issue_99_vd_expiry_s3_dic_issue_99", "target": "aigen_backend_docs_bug_analysis_issue_99_vd_expiry_s3_dic_bug_3_need_action_vs_waiting_vendor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bug-analysis-issue-99-vd-expiry-s3-dic.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "aigen_backend_docs_bug_analysis_issue_99_vd_expiry_s3_dic_issue_99", "target": "aigen_backend_docs_bug_analysis_issue_99_vd_expiry_s3_dic_bug_4_card_grouping", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bug-analysis-issue-99-vd-expiry-s3-dic.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "aigen_backend_docs_bug_analysis_issue_99_vd_expiry_s3_dic_bug_1_dic_detail_sequence_mixing", "target": "aigen_backend_docs_bug_analysis_issue_99_vd_expiry_s3_dic_list_item_rfq_dic", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bug-analysis-iss